course: dictionary
lesson: 11683
title: A legend with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Atlantis is a proper noun, a special name for one thing, so it always starts with a capital letter, like the name of a person or a city. It is the name of a legendary island city, not a place you can find on a modern map. «Atlantis sank under the sea in one day and night.» The word sank tells you the city went down under the water.
explain: The story of Atlantis comes from Plato, a Greek writer who lived a very long time ago. Stories like this are called myths. Many people still search for Atlantis, but no one has found proof that it really existed. «Explorers have searched the seas for Atlantis for hundreds of years.» The search goes on, but the answer is still a mystery.
explain: Plato may have made up Atlantis to teach a lesson about pride. Stories often carry a message like that. When you read a story, ask what it is trying to teach you as well as what happens in it.
explain: Atlantis is also the name of other things: a NASA space shuttle, some hotels and some games. Use the context to decide which one is meant. «The divers hoped to find Atlantis beneath the waves» is about the lost city, not a hotel.
fact: Atlantis is a proper noun, so it always has a capital A.
fact: «Atlantis» means a legendary island city that sank under the sea in one day and night, in a story by Plato.
fact: In stories and films, «Atlantis» means a lost, wonderful underwater city.
fact: «Atlantis» is also the name of a NASA space shuttle, some hotels and some games.
fact: A myth is an old story that people tell; there is no evidence that Atlantis really existed.
exercise: «The explorers searched the sea for the lost city of Atlantis.» What is Atlantis in this sentence? | A space shuttle that flies into space | A real island where people live today | *A legendary city that sank under the sea | A hotel by the beach
exercise: Why does Atlantis start with a capital letter? | *Because it is a proper noun, the special name of one thing | Because it is at the start of a sentence in every case | Because it is a long word | Because it is a question
exercise: «The Atlantis hotel had a pool shaped like a shell.» What does Atlantis mean here? | A lost underwater city | *The name of a hotel | A long, old story about pride | A kind of fish
test: «Plato told a story about a city that sank in one day and night.» What do we call a story like this if no one has proof it really happened? | Recipe | *Myth | Fact | Diary entry
test: «The divers hoped to find Atlantis beneath the waves.» Which meaning fits this sentence best? | A school in town | A tall mountain | *A lost, wonderful underwater city | A kind of game
exam: Which words in «Some people think Atlantis is real, but there is no evidence it existed» show that Atlantis is probably a myth? | Some people think | is real | *no evidence it existed | a space shuttle
